{"bookId": "CB_79T9od9nkEF26iS6gX2klCI5", "title": "Flowers For Algernon", "bookmarks": {"synckey": 1732334215, "updated": [{"bookId": "CB_79T9od9nkEF26iS6gX2klCI5", "bookmarkId": "CB_79T9od9nkEF26iS6gX2klCI5_19_42384-42646", "createTime": 1732323560, "range": "42384-42646", "markText": "Alice knows everything about me now, and accepts the fact that we can be together for only a short while. She has agreed to go away when I tell her to go. It's painful to think about that, but what we have, I suspect, is more than most people find in a lifetime.", "colorStyle": 4, "type": 1, "chapterUid": 19}, {"bookId": "CB_79T9od9nkEF26iS6gX2klCI5", "bookmarkId": "CB_79T9od9nkEF26iS6gX2klCI5_13_76929-77370", "createTime": 1730221101, "range": "76929-77370", "markText": "She stared down at the bride and groom on the wedding cake she was decorating and I could see her lips barely move as she whispered: \"It was evil when Adam and Eve ate from the tree of knowledge. It was evil when they saw they was naked, and learned about lust and shame. And they was driven out of Paradise and the gates was closed to them. If not for that none of us would have to grow old and be sick and die.\"", "colorStyle": 4, "type": 1, "chapterUid": 13}], "removed": [], "chapters": [{"title": "Flowers For Algernon", "chapterUid": 19, "chapterIdx": 19}, {"title": "Flowers For Algernon", "chapterUid": 13, "chapterIdx": 13}], "book": {"bookId": "CB_79T9od9nkEF26iS6gX2klCI5", "version": 842332138, "format": "epub", "soldout": 0, "bookStatus": 1, "cover": "https://res.weread.qq.com/wrepub/CB_5gv6cj6eF2Rs6i86go4pW8i2_parsecover", "title": "Flowers For Algernon", "author": "Daniel Keyes", "coverBoxInfo": {"colorsPure": ["#93B0DA", "#98B8DD"]}}}, "reviews": {"reviews": [{"reviewId": "17408780_7VUIlH1XQ", "review": {"isPrivate": 1, "bookId": "CB_79T9od9nkEF26iS6gX2klCI5", "content": "It is a pleasure, but also a curse to be smart.", "star": 100, "type": 4, "bookVersion": 842332138, "reviewId": "17408780_7VUIlH1XQ", "u